       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, and seizures. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so I don't see anything that would justify it.\n\nWas this a typo? Typical adult doses are:\n- **Depression, OCD, or other indications:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose you want, for example 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 600 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first. I can add a note to the order if you'd like."
